<Doc lang="en" title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using spacering.net and a SpaceRing account." paths={paths} updated="October 6, 2026">
  <p>These terms apply when you use spacering.net and sign in to a SpaceRing account. By signing in you accept them.</p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>SpaceRing is in its early days. Today an account gives you a ring number and lets you sign in; the products described on the site (Space, the personal assistant, Harness, Relay and Signet) are plans and concept previews, not services you can use yet. Codeg is open-source software published under its own license. We may change, pause or end parts of the service.</p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sign in only with accounts that are yours: one SpaceRing account per person.</li>
    <li>Keep your GitHub or Google account secure. Whoever controls it can sign in as you.</li>
    <li>Ring numbers are given in the order accounts are created. They cannot be chosen, transferred or sold, and are never given out again.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not use the service to break the law, to attack or overload it, to get into accounts that are not yours, or to create accounts automatically.</p>

  <h2>Ending</h2>
  <p>You can stop at any time and ask us to delete your account (see the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>). We may suspend or close accounts that break these terms.</p>

  <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>The service is provided as it is, without warranties. To the extent the law allows, SpaceRing is not liable for indirect or consequential losses arising from its use.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>When these terms change, the date above changes with it. Significant changes are announced on the site before they apply; using the service after that means you accept them.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:privacy@spacering.net">privacy@spacering.net</a></p>
</Doc>
